Files:
 corpus/suhrawardy-1905.jsonl
 corpus/recovered.tsv
 corpus/proofed.tsv
 corpus/corrections.tsv
 corpus/artefacts.tsv
Copyright: 1905 Abdullah al-Mamun al-Suhrawardy
License: public-domain
Comment:
 "The Sayings of Muhammad", collected and translated by Abdullah al-Mamun
 al-Suhrawardy, first published in 1905. Source scan:
 https://archive.org/details/the-sayings-of-muhammad_202401
 .
 The scan is of a later reprint, and only the 1905 sayings themselves are
 taken from it. The reprint's preface and introduction are under their own
 copyright and are excluded by the parser; no part of them is in this
 package.
 .
 recovered.tsv, proofed.tsv, corrections.tsv and artefacts.tsv hold nothing
 but readings of that same public-domain text: sayings the OCR destroyed,
 transcribed from the page images, and the anchored repairs that undo
 scanning damage. They are transcription and carry no separate copyright
 claim; they are listed here so that every file is accounted for.

Files:
 corpus/suhrawardy-modern.jsonl
 corpus/modernised.tsv
 corpus/modern-lexicon.tsv
Copyright: 2026 Masroor Ahmad <debian@masroor.de>
License: CC0-1.0
Comment:
 A modernisation of the 1905 English: "pays" for "payeth", "you" for "thou",
 and 64 hand-written rewrites where no word-level substitution was enough.
 The 1905 wording is kept beside it in corpus/suhrawardy-1905.jsonl, so the
 whole of the change is a diff.
 .
 The underlying text being in the public domain, this work is the author's
 own and is dedicated to the public domain in turn.

