Copyright: 2026 Masroor Ahmad <debian@masroor.de>
License: GPL-3.0+

License: public-domain
 Abdullah al-Mamun al-Suhrawardy died in 1935 and the book was published in
 1905. Copyright has therefore expired in every jurisdiction relevant to
 Debian's distribution of it:
 .
   * United States: published before 1930, so in the public domain there
     regardless of any formality.
   * Germany, and the European Union generally: 70 years post mortem
     auctoris, which elapsed at the end of 2005.
   * United Kingdom, where the book was published: likewise 70 years p.m.a.
 .
 The translation is the part that could carry a copyright of its own, and it
 is Suhrawardy's; the sayings he was translating are older still. No estate
 or successor holds any right in it.

